5. §5.6 Storage-cache trim: skip_indexes load mode + index-build skip when
   only query-jit consumes the plan (gated kernel_path == NONE).
6. §5.7 scan_qjit_temp replacement scan: third branch in
   TempCollectionReplacementScan serving qjit_temps_ directly (string_t
   views into the QjitTable arena); CDC write-back deleted from the
   query-jit store path. Dual temp materialization gone.
7. §5.5 j>e investigation => verdict: A+ JOIN-FILTER PUSHDOWN (user chose
   A+ over A/B/C and over lingo-db's PK-side-only variant).
   Implementation:
   - Build-side key-0 min/max accumulated in Finalize's existing link walk
     (thread-local + CAS merge; empty HT => min>max drops all). Runtime
     symbols qjit_ht_key0_min/max, qjit_ht_entries; QjitHashTable gains
     key0_offset ctor param (= ht prefix_bytes, plumbed as
     QjitCompiled::ht_key0_offsets).
   - PlanJoinFilterPushdown (query_jit_steps.cpp Pass D, post-resolution):
     stable cheap-before-expensive filter reorder in the pre-probe prefix
     (expensive = any string predicate); Guard per probe whose keys are
     all step-source columns; guard.membership set when expensive filters
     run between guard point and probe. Kill switch
     AQP_QJIT_NO_JOINFILTER. Guards serialized into the §5.1 cache key.
   - Codegen (CompileQuerySteps): loop-invariant lo/hi/entries in the
     morsel entry block; at guard_pos a per-row key range check
     (NULL key drops via load_key_i64_or_skip) + existence pre-probe
     (exact probe match predicate, first match suffices) runtime-gated on
     entries <= 65536.
   - Block skip: per-2048-row min/max over the guarded key column
     (executor GetBlockStats, memoized per table.col, all-NULL block =>
     {INT32_MAX, INT32_MIN}); delivered via QjitQueryContext::user
     (array of const int32_t* per step — QjitColView is DuckDB-shared ABI
     and must not grow); two-level morsel loop skips disjoint blocks.
     Both array and entry are null-checked => module is
     stats-availability-independent (cache-key safe).
   - Correctness basis: filters reference only step-source columns,
     inner-join probes commute with filters, guards drop only rows their
     probe would drop.
   Results (top-10 loser queries, node-based, 7 repeats, medians):
   execute -64 ms vs A+ off (9d -19.6, 22d -11.0, 7c -10.5);
   jit_compile +37 ms (larger modules, ~3.7 ms/query — hidden under spec
