### Archived from CLAUDE.md: "Current state" pipeline-jit details (2026-06-15)

`--jit-level=pipeline` compiles, per probe pipeline:
- **Single hash-join probes**: `CompileFilterProbeProjectFusion` — one LLVM
  function per HJ doing filter + HT probe + projection on the probe chunk.
  Registered per-eid in `pipeline_fns`, dispatched in
  `physical_hash_join.cpp:ExecuteInternal`.
- **Consecutive HJ chains (N-probe)**: `CompileMultiProbeChain` — the whole
  chain fused into one function (inspired by lingo-db's single-function
  pipeline compilation): SSA-threaded columns, no intermediate
  materialization, per-stage skip_hash_cmp and payload pruning. Dispatched
  at the innermost HJ; outer HJs are passthrough.
  `--single-column-int-join-mode` (default ON) bypasses DuckDB's
  perfect/array hash join for chain members.
- Full NULL-validity semantics (input masks, HT row validity prefix, NULL
  keys never match, output mask writes).

### Archived from CLAUDE.md: Query-jit architecture details (2026-06-15)

Phases 0-5 of `--jit-level=query` are complete and gated. Architecture:
per sub-query, the adapter Prepares (DuckDB optimizer) → ConvertPlanToIR →
`AnnotateBuildSides` (physical-plan build/probe sides →
`SimplestJoin::build_child`) → `AnalyzeQueryJit`/`BuildExecutionSteps`
(src/qjit/query_jit_steps.cpp, three-pass) → `CompileQuerySteps`
(src/jit/ir_to_llvm.cpp, ONE module + ONE entry fn, morsel body per step)
→ `QjitExecutor::Run` over `QjitWorkerPool`. Any reject ⇒ whole
sub-query on the DuckDB interpreter. Temps: dual-materialized as
`qjit_temps_` QjitTable (compiled consumers, POSITIONAL column
resolution) + `scan_qjit_temp` serves interpreter consumers directly
(§5.7). Reject distribution on JOB after §5.2: 3× `plan-empty-result`,
1× `exception` (pre-existing 10c converter cast).

Storage-plan ruling: only TWO consumers exist — kernel-path
(CSR/sorted/dimension paths, all gated `kernel_path != NONE`) and
query-jit (`qjit_storage_plan_`, FlatTable column data ONLY). §5.6
lazy-skip implemented.

§5.5 A+ join-filter pushdown: build-key-0 min/max range guards +
HT-membership pre-probe (runtime-gated ≤65536 entries) +
cheap-before-expensive filter reorder + per-2048-row block skipping.
Kill switch `AQP_QJIT_NO_JOINFILTER`. Routine `[AQP-QJIT]` traces are
NDEBUG-only since 2026-06-12.

### Archived from CLAUDE.md: Timing/benchmark infrastructure (2026-06-15)

- The timing CSV is always rectangular: JIT-level runs emit the jit_compile
  column (0.000) even when registration is skipped. Sites:
  `duckdb_adapter.cpp` ExecuteSQL ×2 + ExecuteSQLandCreateTempTable,
  `ir_query_splitter.cpp` SetJITFlags fallback.
- `--jit-cache` (default OFF) gates the in-memory JIT object cache.
