§6.1 Bloom-tagged hash-table chain pointers — COMPLETE.
Always-on (no CLI flag). Heads-only tagging; `ir_to_llvm.h:bloom_tag_`.
Directory type changed from `atomic<Entry*>[]` to `atomic<uintptr_t>[]`.
Low 16 bits = OR of bloomMasks[hash>>53] for all entries in chain;
high bits = pointer << 16. Codegen loads i64 tagged word, bloom-filters
with AND+CMP, then untags with LShr(16). Entry::next is plain pointer
(unchanged). bloomMasks[2048] table in query_jit_runtime.cpp (copied
from lingo-db). Performance: net-neutral on JOB (9.8ms / 0.18%).
