§6.4 11d-class gap investigation — RESOLVED.
Root cause: systemic per-row execution overhead in query-jit vs DuckDB's
vectorized interpreter (1.52x at ~99ns/row vs ~65ns/row). Not specific
to 11d/9d/16b. Machine: 6 physical cores, 12 HT threads. 87/678
sub-queries: interp exe faster (303ms total gap). 474/678: qjit exe
faster (5344ms advantage). 68/87 would flip if exe matched interp.
Actionable follow-ups: §6.11 SIMD scan, §6.12 inline sinks.

