§6.12 Tighter morsel entry: inline fast-path HT append — COMPLETE
(2026-06-18). Compiled morsel body now stack-allocates a
QjitHtAppendHandle and calls qjit_ht_begin once at morsel entry. The
hot loop does an inline bump-pointer check (cursor + stride <= limit);
on the fast path no function call is needed. When the chunk is exhausted
the slow path calls qjit_ht_append_slow, which allocates a new chunk
and refreshes the handle. qjit_ht_end writes the cursor back at morsel
exit. ABI struct: QjitHtAppendHandle {cursor, limit, stride, count}
(query_jit_abi.h). Runtime: QjitBuffer::BackChunkState/CommitBackChunk,
QjitHashTable::BeginAppend/AppendRowSlow/EndAppend
(query_jit_runtime.h/cpp). Codegen: ir_to_llvm.cpp CompileQuerySteps
HtBuild sink — fast/slow BasicBlocks with PHI merge for row pointer.
Registered symbols: qjit_ht_begin, qjit_ht_append_slow, qjit_ht_end
(duckdb_adapter.cpp:RegisterQjitRuntimeSymbols).
