### §7.3c — Disk-backed ObjCache + split=none plan replay (2026-06-25)

Two features extending --jit-cache=full:

1. Disk-backed ObjCache: compiled .o files persist to /dev/shm/aqp_jit_cache/v1/
   (tmpfs, RAM speed, survives process restart, cleared on reboot). File format:
   <dir>/<16-char-hex-hash>.o, raw ELF bytes. Write via atomic .tmp.PID + rename().
   On cache miss, TryCacheLoad checks disk after in-memory miss and promotes to
   in-memory ObjCache. InstallCacheHook writes to disk after LLVM compilation.
   Optional --jit-cache-dir=<path> overrides default directory.
   Works for ALL jit levels (none/expr/operator/pipeline/query) × ALL splits.

2. Split=none query-jit plan replay: intercept at aqp_middleware.cpp before
   adapter->ExecuteSQL(sql). Iter 0 records via BeginPlanRecording(); iter 1+
   checks QueryPlanCache and calls ReplayQjitFinal() directly, skipping the
   entire ParseSQL+Optimize+ConvertPlanToIR+AnalyzeQueryJit+BuildExecutionSteps
   pipeline (~444 ms/iter saved). Non-query-jit split=none benefits only from
   disk ObjCache (no splitter overhead to skip — the 403 ms is DuckDB
   Prepare+RegisterJIT cost).

