so tuned configs with mixed JIT levels/compile-modes see lower cache
hit rates than uniform configs. Accepted as-is (option 1: just measure).

### LLVM initialization thread-safety fix (2026-06-25)

EnsureLLVMInit() used a plain `static bool` guard — not thread-safe.
When cross-query latency hiding runs PrepareNextQuery on a background
thread, both the main thread and bg thread can create IrToLlvmCompiler
instances concurrently. If both see `llvm_initialized == false`, both
call InitializeNativeTarget(), registering x86-64 twice. LLVM's
TargetRegistry::RegisterTarget is documented as not thread-safe.
Symptom: intermittent "Cannot choose between targets x86-64 and x86-64"
LLJIT creation error (race window depends on binary layout/timing).

Fix: replaced with `std::call_once(llvm_init_flag, ...)` which
guarantees exactly-once execution with full thread safety.
Location: src/jit/ir_to_llvm.cpp:253-259.

