### §7.3 Bug fix: plan recording for speculative/cross-query paths (2026-06-26)

`--jit-cache=full` plan replay was broken in two cases:

**Bug 1 — spec-jit HIT path:** When spec-jit got a HIT for a subquery,
`ExecuteSpeculativeAndCreateTempTable` was called instead of
`ExecuteSQLandCreateTempTable`. The speculative function had no
`plan_recording_active_` recording, so one subquery entry was missing
from the cached plan. The code at save time (`cached.final_query =
buf.back()`) then treated the WRONG entry as the final query, corrupting
the cached plan structure. Symptom: "Table with name tempN does not
exist!" errors on the replay iteration.

**Bug 2 — cross-query latency hiding path:** For non-query-jit configs
with node-based split, the cross-query prep path called
`ExecuteSpeculativeAndCreateTempTable` for the first subquery, then
manually recorded the entry in the splitter (ir_query_splitter.cpp
:2414-2422). After Bug 1's fix added recording inside
`ExecuteSpeculativeAndCreateTempTable`, this created a double recording —
first an entry with empty SQL (from inside the function, since sql=""
was the default parameter), then the correct entry from the splitter.
Symptom: "No statement to prepare!" on replay iteration for all queries
after the first (only in benchmark mode with all 113 queries).

Fix: Added `const std::string &sql` parameter + plan recording block to
`ExecuteSpeculativeAndCreateTempTable` (duckdb_adapter.cpp:2045-2053).
Both call sites now pass `sub_sql`: spec-jit HIT path
(ir_query_splitter.cpp:2490) and cross-query prep path (:2387).
Removed the redundant manual recording from the cross-query path.

Files changed:
- include/adapters/duckdb_adapter.h — added sql parameter
- src/adapters/duckdb_adapter.cpp — added sql parameter + recording
- src/split/ir_query_splitter.cpp — passed sub_sql at both call sites,
  removed redundant manual recording

## §7.1 Direct CDC scan in query-jit — DEPRIORITIZED
Date: 2026-06-26

CDC→QjitTable conversion costs 540 ms across 113 JOB queries (measured
2026-06-20), NOT the 1.5 s originally estimated. More importantly, if
per-subquery tuning is restricted to query-jit-only configs (§7.4), ALL
sub-queries produce `QjitTable` directly (`duckdb_adapter.cpp:1635`),
so NO CDC conversion occurs and this optimization is unnecessary.

§7.1 only matters if mixed-config tuning (interp/expr/pipeline +
query-jit) is needed. Since query-jit-only tuning saves only 0.11 s
less than pure TPDE (§7.4 analysis), and the mixed-config tuning's CDC
cost (540 ms) exceeds its execution savings (429 ms), §7.1 is
deprioritized in favor of §7.2 and §7.3.

